7. Adafruit library sketches — repository test fixtures, NOT in the
   published package
   Files: test/sim/engine/__fixtures__/adafruit_ssd1306.hex,
   adafruit_bmp280.hex, adafruit_dht22.hex and adafruit_dht11.hex

   Each is built from the sketch beside it (the .ino of the same name) by
   devolt's in-browser avr-gcc (gcc-avr 7.3.0+Atmel3.7.0) for the Arduino
   Uno, against these libraries, whose object code it may contain:

   - Adafruit SSD1306 2.5.13 (adafruit_ssd1306.hex)
     Copyright (c) 2012, Adafruit Industries. License: BSD-3-Clause.
   - Adafruit GFX Library 1.12.1 (adafruit_ssd1306.hex)
     Copyright (c) 2012 Adafruit Industries. License: BSD-2-Clause.
   - Adafruit BMP280 Library 2.6.8 (adafruit_bmp280.hex)
     Copyright (c) Adafruit Industries. License: BSD (the library's
     header: "BSD license, all text above must be included in any
     redistribution").
   - Adafruit Unified Sensor 1.1.15 (adafruit_bmp280.hex)
     Copyright (c) Adafruit Industries. License: Apache-2.0.
   - Adafruit BusIO 1.17.0 (adafruit_ssd1306.hex, adafruit_bmp280.hex)
     Copyright (c) 2017 Adafruit Industries. License: MIT.
   - DHT sensor library 1.4.6 (adafruit_dht22.hex, adafruit_dht11.hex)
     Copyright (c) 2020 Adafruit Industries. License: MIT.
   - ArduinoCore-avr 1.8.6, its core and the Wire library (all four)
     Copyright (c) Arduino LLC and contributors.
     License: LGPL-2.1-or-later.
   - avr-libc (BSD-3-Clause) and libgcc (GPL-3.0-or-later WITH
     GCC-exception-3.1), as any avr-gcc build links them.

   The licence texts are in test/sim/engine/__fixtures__/LICENSES/, one
   file per library (the LGPL-2.1 text and avr-libc's terms included).

   Bundled so the engine and Rust core suites run a real library's bus
   traffic against the part models. The library sources are those of the
   upstream releases named (github.com/adafruit/<library> at the version
   tag; github.com/arduino/ArduinoCore-avr tag 1.8.6), and the sketch
   beside each hex rebuilds it with them, so the LGPL object code can be
   relinked against a modified core. The package tarball excludes `test/`, and
   the Rust core reads the hex only in its tests (`include_str!` under
   `#[cfg(test)]`), so none of this code ships in the npm package or the
   WebAssembly module.
